            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 13:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Hear now my reasoning, and hearken to the pleadings of my lips.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 13:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Will ye speak wickedly for God? and talk deceitfully for him?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 13:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Will ye accept his person? will ye contend for God?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 13:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Is it good that he should search you out? or as one man mocketh another, do ye so mock him?",
